    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (3/3 passing, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization applied whenever an owner is created, in the Spring Boot PetClinic REST app.\n\n**New component** \u2014 `rest/validation/AddressNormalizer.java` (following the existing `TelephoneNormalizer` pattern):\n- Trims and collapses whitespace to single spaces\n- Upper-cases the value\n- Expands whole-word abbreviations: `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`\n- Returns `\"\"` for a `null`/blank input so callers can treat it uniformly as missing\n\n**Wired into `OwnerRestControllerV1`:**\n1. Injected `AddressNormalizer` via the constructor.\n2. In `normalizeAndValidate`, the address is normalized and written back onto the payload **before** the required-field check \u2014 so the stored and returned `address` is the normalized form, and an address that is blank after normalization is rejected (400) by the existing `validateRequiredFields`.\n3. `findHouseholdMembers` (duplicate detection) now compares addresses using the normalized form on both the payload and each existing owner.\n4. `generateHouseholdId` (shared household id) now derives its key from the normalized address.\n\nJavadoc was updated to reflect the new behavior. All three acceptance tests pass:\n- `coreNormalizesWhitespaceAndCase`: `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`\n- `functionalityExpandsAbbreviations`: `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`\n- `errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize`: `\"   \"` \u2192 400 Bad Request",
